<title>USA: Goodyear calls patent ruling erroneous.</title>
<headline>Goodyear calls patent ruling erroneous.</headline>
<dateline>AKRON, Ohio 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goodyear Tire &amp; Rubber Co said Thursday it was appealing a court decision that rival Hercules Tire &amp; Rubber Co did not infringe on one of its design patents.</p>
<p>It called the ruling &quot;erroneous.&quot;  </p>
<p>&quot;We believe the court ruled erroneously on the issue of infringement, and with that decision, unduly limited the scope of Goodyear's design patent,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>&quot;Goodyear successfully established that tire tread patterns are proper subject matter for design patent protection,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>The company said it would continue to aggressively protect its intellectual property rights.</p>
</text>
